body:
#122745 ended up being merged, so this PR will now (if rebased/merged) trigger deprecation warnings due to relying on `RayResult::collider` and `ShapeResult::collider`.

You'll need to change these methods:

- `PhysicsIntersectPointResult2D::get_collider`
- `PhysicsIntersectRayResult2D::get_collider`
- `PhysicsIntersectShapeResult2D::get_collider`
- `PhysicsIntersectPointResult3D::get_collider`
- `PhysicsIntersectRayResult3D::get_collider`
- `PhysicsIntersectShapeResult3D::get_collider`

... to not do this:

```cpp
Object *PhysicsIntersectRayResult3D::get_collider() const {
    return result.collider;
}
```

... but instead do something like this:

```cpp
Object *PhysicsIntersectRayResult3D::get_collider() const {
    if (result.collider_id.is_valid()) {
        return ObjectDB::get_instance(result.collider_id);
    }

    return nullptr;
}
```

(The `is_valid` check isn't strictly necessary, and as mentioned in #122745 I might try to remove them at some later point, but this is at least consistent with [`KinematicCollision*D::get_collider`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6a0f6f32cfb2ce4cc5bad6641d0afda413b62a9d/scene/3d/physics/kinematic_collision_3d.cpp#L78-L85) and [`RayCast*D::get_collider`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6a0f6f32cfb2ce4cc5bad6641d0afda413b62a9d/scene/3d/physics/ray_cast_3d.cpp#L88-L94).)

~~So something like this: https://github.com/mihe/godot/commit/34378eb517d325abb8ff59c567c6bd2a30643aa4~~

**EDIT:** I forgot that this ideally needs to try to grab from `collider` when `#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED`, similar to how `PhysicsDirectSpaceState*D::_intersect_point` and the other `Dictionary`-returning methods are doing it. However, this could probably do with a helper method to better isolate the deprecation stuff. I'll put up a PR for it.

It might be possible to add in future with a default argument, without breaking compat:

e.g.
```
int get_num_hits() const;
Vector3 get_position(int p_index = 0) const;
.. etc
```
@AThousandShips is quite expert with this kind of breakage, would this work?
